IMPORT prelude

-- Town Councils Act 1988 (Singapore) -- what HDB residents meet: lift upgrading polls and improvement contributions
-- (Part 4A, ss 29 to 36), the charge and power of sale for unpaid conservancy charges (s 66), and the vehicle owner's
-- liability for parking offences (s 70).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/TCA1988.txt.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 27 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository, 16 of them for s 4 (a Town Council's
-- establishment): other Acts make Town Councils responsible for common property. SCOPED to the money and liability a
-- resident meets. Not encoded: establishment and constitution, members and conflicts, functions and by-laws, proceedings,
-- the Town Council Fund and accounts, compliance reviews and official management, and the HDB-Town Council relationship.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Town Councils Act 1988 -- residents`

§§ `31 -- the lift upgrading poll`

-- s 31(3): a Town Council may carry out lift upgrading works in a building "if, and only if -- (a) ... the total VOTING
-- VALUE of votes in favour ... is at least 75% of the total voting value of votes of ALL such owners; and (b) the Minister
-- approves". (2)(b): the poll is of owners of flats "the occupants of which directly benefit". (5): HDB votes for unsold
-- flats. (4): a poll is not invalid for procedural failure if the principles were followed and the result unaffected.
--
-- The threshold is 75% of all eligible owners' voting value -- not of votes cast. Abstention counts against.
GIVEN `voting value in favour` IS A NUMBER, `total voting value of all eligible owners` IS A NUMBER, `the Minister approves` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lift upgrading may proceed` IF
        (`voting value in favour` TIMES 4) AT LEAST (`total voting value of all eligible owners` TIMES 3)
    AND `the Minister approves`

§§ `32, 33 -- who pays, and how much`

-- s 32(2): on completion the Town Council "may recover, by way of improvement contributions, the costs ... from every owner"
-- of the benefiting flats -- including those who voted against. (3): the amount is determined by the Town Council "whose
-- decision is final". (4): it "must NOT BE LESS THAN the improvement contribution that the Board might have determined" for
-- similar works.
-- (5): "owner" means the owner "at the time the improvement contribution is DETERMINED".
-- s 33(1): pay within one month of a written demand. (2): where no representation has been taken out for a deceased owner,
-- or the personal representatives fail to seek HDB consent to transfer, the Town Council may require "the SPOUSE (if any) ...
-- or any BENEFICIARY of his or her estate who has attained the age of 21 years to pay ... as if it is a debt owed by him or
-- her".
--
-- (4) is a floor, not a cap: the contribution may exceed what HDB would have charged, never fall below it. And because
-- liability attaches at determination, a buyer who completes after the works but before the determination pays for works
-- done before they bought.
DECLARE Contribution HAS
    `the amount determined` IS A NUMBER
    `what HDB would have determined` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the contribution` IS A Contribution
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the amount is within section 32(4)` IF
    `the contribution`'s `the amount determined` AT LEAST `the contribution`'s `what HDB would have determined`

GIVEN `owned the flat when the contribution was determined` IS A BOOLEAN, `voted against` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person must pay the contribution` IF
    `owned the flat when the contribution was determined`

DECLARE Relation IS ONE OF
    `the surviving spouse`
    `an adult beneficiary`
    `a beneficiary under 21`
    `a neighbour`

GIVEN `the relation` IS A Relation, `the estate has no representation or the representatives did not seek transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Town Council may require the person to pay as their own debt` IF
        `the estate has no representation or the representatives did not seek transfer`
    AND CONSIDER `the relation`
        WHEN `the surviving spouse` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an adult beneficiary` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `34, 66 -- the charge on the flat and the power of sale`

-- s 34(1): an improvement contribution unpaid "3 MONTHS after" a written demand becomes "a charge on the flat". s 66(1):
-- conservancy and service charges unpaid "90 DAYS after" a written demand do the same.
-- s 34(5), 66(2): the Town Council then "has the power of sale ... as if the Town Council is a registered mortgagee, EVEN THOUGH
-- THE CHARGE IS NOT REGISTERED". s 34(6), 66(4): sale only after notice of 90 days (with HDB's approval), and (s 34(6)(c)) no
-- pending legal action. s 34(7), 66(5): not if the owner's movable property in the flat would cover the debt.
-- s 34(4), 66(3): the charge ranks behind prior registered encumbrances, HDB lease moneys and the CPF charge.
-- s 34(9): the purchaser need not inquire into the regularity of the sale.
--
-- A flat can be sold for unpaid conservancy charges. The steps run: demand; 90 days; charge; notice of sale; 90 more days.
DECLARE Arrears HAS
    `kind` IS A STRING
    `days since the written demand` IS A NUMBER
    `days since the notice of sale` IS A NUMBER
    `HDB approved the sale` IS A BOOLEAN
    `legal action to restrain the sale is pending` IS A BOOLEAN
    `movable property in the flat would cover the debt` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the arrears` IS AN Arrears
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the arrears are a charge on the flat` IF
    `the arrears`'s `days since the written demand` GREATER THAN 90

GIVEN `the arrears` IS AN Arrears
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Town Council may sell the flat` IF
        `the arrears are a charge on the flat` `the arrears`
    AND `the arrears`'s `days since the notice of sale` GREATER THAN 90
    AND `the arrears`'s `HDB approved the sale`
    AND NOT `the arrears`'s `legal action to restrain the sale is pending`
    AND NOT `the arrears`'s `movable property in the flat would cover the debt`

-- (For improvement contributions s 34(1) says "3 months"; for conservancy charges s 66(1) says "90 days". The encoding uses
-- 90 days for both; the two are not the same length in every quarter.)

§§ `35 -- where the sale money goes`

-- s 35, in order: (a) costs of sale; (b) the CPF Board's charge; (c) HDB lease moneys; (d) HDB's improvement-contribution
-- charge and the Town Council's charge, in their order of priority; (e) conservancy charges and unsecured improvement
-- contributions owed to the Town Council, EQUALLY; (f) HDB's unsecured improvement contributions; (g) later mortgages; (h)
-- the residue to the owner.
DECLARE Payee IS ONE OF
    `costs of the sale`
    `the CPF Board's charge`
    `HDB lease moneys`
    `secured improvement contributions`
    `conservancy charges and unsecured Town Council contributions`
    `HDB unsecured contributions`
    `a later bank mortgage`
    `the owner`

GIVEN `the payee` IS A Payee
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the order of payment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the payee`
    WHEN `costs of the sale` THEN 1
    WHEN `the CPF Board's charge` THEN 2
    WHEN `HDB lease moneys` THEN 3
    WHEN `secured improvement contributions` THEN 4
    WHEN `conservancy charges and unsecured Town Council contributions` THEN 5
    WHEN `HDB unsecured contributions` THEN 6
    WHEN `a later bank mortgage` THEN 7
    WHEN `the owner` THEN 8

§§ `70 -- parking offences`

-- s 70(1): the vehicle's owner at the time "shall be guilty of an offence ... as if the person were the actual offender",
-- unless the vehicle was stolen or illegally taken. (3): not guilty if the owner (a) within 7 DAYS after the notice names
-- the person in charge by STATUTORY DECLARATION; or (b), (c) shows they could not with reasonable diligence find out who
-- it was. (5): "A statutory declaration which relates to MORE THAN ONE parking offence is not regarded as a statutory
-- declaration" for (3)(a).
--
-- One declaration per ticket: a single declaration naming the driver for three tickets saves the owner from none.
DECLARE Ticket HAS
    `the vehicle was stolen or illegally taken` IS A BOOLEAN
    `declared the driver within 7 days` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the declaration covers more than one offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `could not with reasonable diligence identify the driver` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the ticket` IS A Ticket
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner is liable for the parking offence` IF
        NOT `the ticket`'s `the vehicle was stolen or illegally taken`
    AND NOT (`the ticket`'s `declared the driver within 7 days` AND NOT `the ticket`'s `the declaration covers more than one offence`)
    AND NOT `the ticket`'s `could not with reasonable diligence identify the driver`
